message:<<^id:msg_001|role:user|ts:2026-02-28T18:30:00Z|content:I want to drive from Detroit to Nashville. What is the best route?^>>
message:<<^id:msg_002|role:agent|ts:2026-02-28T18:30:18Z|content:The most popular route is I-75 South to I-24 West — about 9 hours without stops. Would you like suggestions for stops along the way?^>>
message:<<^id:msg_003|role:user|ts:2026-02-28T18:31:45Z|content:Yes please. We like hiking and good food.^>>
message:<<^id:msg_004|role:agent|ts:2026-02-28T18:32:10Z|content:Great choices. I would suggest stopping in Lexington KY for lunch and hitting the Red River Gorge area for a short hike. Then continue south into Nashville for dinner on Broadway.^>>
message:<<^id:msg_005|role:user|ts:2026-02-28T18:38:22Z|content:How long is the Red River Gorge detour?^>>
message:<<^id:msg_006|role:agent|ts:2026-02-28T18:38:41Z|content:About 45 minutes off I-75. Worth every minute. The Natural Bridge trail is under 2 miles and has stunning views.^>>

